From 37b91d12f1cb1c22322022ad315d284054b2c316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dlssg-to-xefg <dev@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:02:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Longshot Vulkan hook failure and swapchain startup crash

1. Adopt pre-existing VkInstance via HookGetInstanceProcAddr:
   Emulators such as Longshot create VkInstance before version.dll/OptiScaler
   and the .asi plugin are loaded, then resolve vkCreateDevice via GIPA.
   Previously s.instances remained empty so CreateDeviceImpl silently skipped
   preparing the device. Now HookGetInstanceProcAddr records any live non-null
   VkInstance (with apiVersion == 0) and PrepareDevice validates Vulkan 1.3
   support directly via physical device properties/features.

2. Prevent swapchain/present crash over detoured short loader stubs:
   Skip MinHook inline detours on optional device-level loader stubs
   (vkCreateSwapchainKHR, vkDestroySwapchainKHR, vkQueuePresentKHR) when they
   are already detoured by OptiScaler/overlays or are short dispatch stubs.

3. Expand VulkanFeatureChain::Size() with common Vulkan 1.3 and EXT feature
   structs used by emulators (mesh shader, robustness2, EDS3, GPL, anti-lag,
   mutable descriptor type, etc.) so PrepareDevice does not refuse valid
   feature chains with feature_chain_unsupported.
---
 src/vulkan/VulkanFeatureChain.h | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/vulkan/VulkanHost.cpp       | 75 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 159 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

